{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are implementing GitHub issue #8 in user/delegate (read it with `gh issue view 8`; spec is #4, \"CI\" bullet under Testing Decisions). Do not delegate further: no subagents, no cursor_run, no delegate tools. Follow the repo's AGENTS.md.\n\nWorking directory: this worktree, branch `8-ci`, based on origin/main.\n\nFile fence: owns `.github/workflows/ci.yml` only. Forbidden: everything else, unless a Linux-only test failure forces a fix; then stop and report it instead of editing.\n\nRequirements:\n- One workflow, triggered on `pull_request` and `push` to `main`. Never `pull_request_target`.\n- One job named exactly `ci` (it is the required status check), `runs-on: ubuntu-latest`, `permissions: contents: read`.\n- Steps: checkout, Rust toolchain with rustfmt+clippy, cargo cache, then `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test`. Live tests are `#[ignore]`d and must stay excluded (do not pass `--ignored` or `--include-ignored`).\n- Allowed actions only: `actions/*` (GitHub-owned), `dtolnay/rust-toolchain`, `Swatinem/rust-cache`. Pin every action by full 40-char commit SHA with a trailing `# vX` comment. Look the SHAs up with `gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/commits/TAG -q .sha` (or the branch `stable` for dtolnay/rust-toolchain); do not invent them.\n- Example of a pinned step line: `- uses: actions/checkout@<40-hex-sha> # v5`\n- Run `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` locally before committing; if either fails on existing code, report it (do not fix outside the fence).\n\nFinish: commit with a conventional message ending `Co-Authored-By: Composer 2.5 <noreply@cursor.com>`. Do not push; the orchestrator pushes.\n\nCompletion bar: report the commit SHA, the SHAs you pinned (with tags), and local fmt/clippy results, or a failure triage — nothing in between. Then **Friction**: up to 3 bullets on what slowed you, what this brief got wrong or left out, what you'd change (\"none\" is fine).\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"57a946cc-91a7-4752-a451-3ee6bfd5841f"}
